-- VariantEquiv fixture (DESIGN.md §9.3): SHA-256 compression in the shapes
-- the elaborator produced for the former QMDB fixture's sha256.rs (removed 2026-10-05; see
-- tests/phase3.rs, `variant_equiv_*`).
--
-- * `ve::compress` is the portable reference: opaque (it contains loops, so
--   the elaborator marks it opaque), its three `for` loops are
--   measure-recursive, opaque loop helpers with irrelevant bound
--   hypotheses, a dependent-match loop guard, `array::set`/`array::index`
--   with bound proofs, and `u32::from_be_bytes`. Every arithmetic proof is a
--   certificate-free `linarith` (the kernel finds the certificate, using
--   the context's hypotheses — the loop bounds and guard equations).
-- * `ve::compress_sha2` is the aarch64 variant, written against the
--   hardware models of sandblaster/targets/core/aarch64.core in the
--   `sha2` crate's instruction sequence (vld1q/vrev32q/vreinterpretq,
--   vaddq with the constants, vsha256hq/vsha256h2q, vsha256su0q/su1q).
-- Load after the prelude and aarch64.core.

def[exec] ve::K : Array U32 64usize :=
